---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { getUi } from '@/lib/i18n'

// en only: availableLocales below says so, and /zh/terms/ and
// /zh/privacy/ do not exist. Read through getUi anyway so the
// anchor label has the same single source as every other surface.
const ui = getUi('en')
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Terms"
    description="Read the terms governing access to Manyfold, including accounts, agent content, acceptable use, billing, and service availability."
    availableLocales={['en']}
>
    <article class="docs-prose-container py-6 md:py-8">
        <header class="mb-4">
            <p class="docs-kicker">Netmind</p>
            <h1 class="mt-3 text-h1" id="page-title">
                Terms of Service
            </h1>
            <p class="mt-2 text-ui text-muted">Last updated: May 5, 2026.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="prose-doc">
            <p>
                These Terms of Service (the "Terms") govern your access to and
                use of Manyfold, including our websites,
                applications, hosted agent runtimes, APIs, integrations,
                documentation, support channels, and related services
                (collectively, the "Services"). The Services are operated by
                NetMind AI LTD ("Netmind", "we", "us", or "our").
            </p>
            <p>
                By accessing or using the Services, you agree to these Terms and
                our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree,
                do not use the Services. If you use the Services on behalf of an
                organization, you represent that you have authority to bind that
                organization to these Terms.
            </p>

            <h2 id="eligibility-and-accounts">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#eligibility-and-accounts"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                1. Eligibility and accounts
            </h2>
            <p>
                You must be at least 18 years old to use the Services. You must
                provide accurate account information, keep it current, and
                protect your login credentials, API keys, connected accounts,
                and other secrets. You are responsible for all activity that
                occurs under your account or organization.
            </p>
            <p>
                You must promptly notify us if you believe your account,
                credentials, agent runtime, or connected service has been
                compromised.
            </p>

            <h2 id="the-services">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#the-services"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                2. The Services
            </h2>
            <p>
                Manyfold lets users create, configure, host, and
                operate AI agents. Agent runtimes may execute code, call tools,
                access repositories or files, connect to third-party services,
                and exchange prompts, outputs, logs, and metadata with AI model
                providers and infrastructure providers.
            </p>
            <p>
                You are responsible for the agents you create, the instructions
                you provide, the tools and credentials you connect, the data you
                upload, and the results of any commands, automations, or
                workflows you run through the Services.
            </p>

            <h2 id="ai-generated-outputs">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#ai-generated-outputs"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                3. AI-generated outputs
            </h2>
            <p>
                AI-generated outputs are automated, probabilistic, and may be
                inaccurate, incomplete, outdated, offensive, or unsuitable for
                your intended use. You must evaluate outputs independently
                before relying on them.
            </p>
            <p>
                The Services do not provide professional legal, medical,
                financial, security, compliance, or other expert advice. You are
                responsible for decisions, actions, and omissions based on agent
                outputs.
            </p>

            <h2 id="your-content">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#your-content"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                4. Your content
            </h2>
            <p>
                "Your Content" means prompts, chat messages, files, code,
                repositories, data, datasets, credentials you submit for use by
                the Services, tool responses, agent configurations, comments,
                feedback, and other materials you upload, import, create, or
                transmit through the Services.
            </p>
            <p>
                As between you and Netmind, you retain ownership of Your
                Content. You grant us and our service providers a worldwide,
                non-exclusive, royalty-free license to host, copy, process,
                transmit, display, modify, and otherwise use Your Content as
                needed to provide, secure, support, maintain, and improve the
                Services and to comply with law.
            </p>
            <p>
                You represent that you have all rights, permissions, notices,
                and consents needed to submit Your Content and to grant the
                license above. You are responsible for ensuring Your Content
                complies with law and does not infringe or violate the rights of
                others.
            </p>

            <h2 id="credentials-integrations-and-end-users">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#credentials-integrations-and-end-users"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                5. Credentials, integrations, and end users
            </h2>
            <p>
                When you connect a model provider, repository, messaging
                channel, API, or other integration, you authorize us to use the
                provided credentials and connection data to perform the actions
                you request through the Services. You are responsible for
                complying with the terms of each connected service.
            </p>
            <p>
                If your agents interact with your own customers, employees,
                contractors, or other end users, you are responsible for giving
                all required notices, obtaining all required consents, handling
                end-user requests, and ensuring your agents are lawful and
                appropriate for their intended audience.
            </p>

            <h2 id="acceptable-use">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#acceptable-use"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                6. Acceptable use
            </h2>
            <p>You must not use the Services to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Violate any law, regulation, contractual duty, or third-party right.</li>
                <li>
                    Upload, generate, distribute, or request illegal, harmful,
                    abusive, harassing, defamatory, hateful, sexually exploitative,
                    or otherwise objectionable content.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Infringe intellectual property, privacy, publicity,
                    confidentiality, or data protection rights.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Access accounts, systems, networks, data, or services without
                    authorization.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Create malware, evade security controls, exfiltrate secrets,
                    perform credential theft, or facilitate cyber abuse.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Overload, disrupt, reverse engineer, scrape, resell, or abuse
                    the Services or their infrastructure.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Misrepresent AI-generated content as human-generated where
                    disclosure is required, impersonate others, or deceive people
                    about an agent's identity or capabilities.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Submit personal data about children or highly sensitive data
                    unless you have a lawful basis and all required consents.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                We may investigate suspected violations and may remove content,
                disable agents, suspend runtimes, revoke access, or terminate
                accounts where we believe it is necessary to protect the
                Services, users, Netmind, or third parties.
            </p>

            <h2 id="third-party-services">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#third-party-services"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                7. Third-party services
            </h2>
            <p>
                The Services may interoperate with third-party services,
                including AI model providers, hosting providers, app stores,
                repositories, payment providers, messaging platforms, and tool
                APIs. Those services are governed by their own terms and privacy
                policies. We are not responsible for third-party services,
                content, policies, availability, security, or outputs.
            </p>

            <h2 id="plans-usage-limits-and-fees">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#plans-usage-limits-and-fees"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                8. Plans, usage limits, and fees
            </h2>
            <p>
                Some Services may be offered under free, invite-only, trial,
                usage-limited, metered, or paid plans. We may apply limits to
                runtime count, compute, storage, token usage, model usage,
                network access, integrations, automations, or other resources.
            </p>
            <p>
                If you purchase a paid plan or incur metered usage, you agree to
                pay all applicable fees, taxes, and charges according to the
                plan, checkout, invoice, or order terms presented to you. Fees
                are non-refundable except where required by law or expressly
                stated in writing.
            </p>

            <h2 id="service-changes-and-availability">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#service-changes-and-availability"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                9. Service changes and availability
            </h2>
            <p>
                We may add, modify, suspend, or discontinue features at any time.
                The Services may include preview, beta, experimental, or
                pre-release features that are provided for evaluation and may be
                changed or removed without notice.
            </p>
            <p>
                We do not guarantee that the Services, agent runtimes, messages,
                files, logs, automations, integrations, or AI outputs will be
                uninterrupted, secure, error-free, accurate, delivered, stored,
                or recoverable.
            </p>

            <h2 id="intellectual-property-and-feedback">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#intellectual-property-and-feedback"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                10. Intellectual property and feedback
            </h2>
            <p>
                We and our licensors retain all rights, title, and interest in
                the Services, including software, infrastructure, models,
                interfaces, designs, documentation, and trademarks. Subject to
                your compliance with these Terms, we grant you a limited,
                revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to use the
                Services for your internal business or personal purposes.
            </p>
            <p>
                If you provide ideas, suggestions, or feedback, you grant us a
                perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free license to use them without
                restriction or compensation.
            </p>

            <h2 id="privacy">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#privacy"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                11. Privacy
            </h2>
            <p>
                Our Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, share, and
                retain personal data. By using the Services, you acknowledge that
                Your Content and usage data may be processed by Netmind and by
                third-party providers as described in the Privacy Policy and as
                needed to provide the Services.
            </p>

            <h2 id="termination">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#termination"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                12. Termination
            </h2>
            <p>
                You may stop using the Services at any time. We may suspend or
                terminate your access to the Services, remove content, disable
                agents, or delete runtimes if you breach these Terms, create
                risk for the Services or others, fail to pay amounts due, or if
                we are required to do so by law.
            </p>
            <p>
                Provisions that by their nature should survive termination will
                survive, including ownership, licenses, payment obligations,
                disclaimers, limitations of liability, indemnity, governing law,
                and dispute provisions.
            </p>

            <h2 id="disclaimers">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#disclaimers"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                13. Disclaimers
            </h2>
            <p>
                To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Services are
                provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any
                kind, whether express, implied, statutory, or otherwise. We
                disclaim all warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
                particular purpose, title, non-infringement, accuracy,
                availability, security, and quiet enjoyment.
            </p>
            <p>
                You are responsible for maintaining backups of important content
                and for validating agent actions before using them in production,
                regulated, safety-critical, or high-impact contexts.
            </p>

            <h2 id="limitation-of-liability">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#limitation-of-liability"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                14. Limitation of liability
            </h2>
            <p>
                Nothing in these Terms limits liability that cannot be limited
                under applicable law, including liability for death or personal
                injury caused by negligence, fraud, or fraudulent
                misrepresentation.
            </p>
            <p>
                To the maximum extent permitted by law, Netmind and its
                affiliates, officers, employees, agents, licensors, and service
                providers will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special,
                consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, loss of profits,
                loss of revenue, loss of goodwill, loss of data, business
                interruption, or the cost of substitute services, even if advised
                of the possibility of such damages.
            </p>

            <h2 id="indemnity">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#indemnity"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                15. Indemnity
            </h2>
            <p>
                To the extent permitted by law, you will defend, indemnify, and
                hold harmless Netmind and its affiliates, officers, employees,
                agents, licensors, and service providers from claims, damages,
                liabilities, losses, costs, and expenses arising out of or
                relating to Your Content, your agents, your integrations, your
                end users, your breach of these Terms, or your violation of law
                or third-party rights.
            </p>

            <h2 id="governing-law-and-jurisdiction">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#governing-law-and-jurisdiction"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                16. Governing law and jurisdiction
            </h2>
            <p>
                These Terms and any dispute or claim arising out of or in
                connection with them are governed by the laws of England and
                Wales. The courts of England and Wales have exclusive
                jurisdiction, except where applicable law gives you mandatory
                rights to bring claims elsewhere.
            </p>

            <h2 id="miscellaneous">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#miscellaneous"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                17. Miscellaneous
            </h2>
            <p>
                These Terms, together with any supplemental terms and policies
                incorporated by reference, are the entire agreement between you
                and us regarding the Services. You may not assign these Terms
                without our prior written consent. We may assign these Terms to
                an affiliate or in connection with a merger, acquisition,
                financing, reorganization, or sale of assets.
            </p>
            <p>
                If any provision is found unenforceable, the remaining
                provisions remain in effect. Our failure to enforce a provision
                is not a waiver. We may update these Terms from time to time.
                Your continued use of the Services after the updated Terms take
                effect means you accept the updated Terms.
            </p>

            <h2 id="contact">
                <a
                    class="docs-heading-anchor"
                    href="#contact"
                    aria-label={ui.headingLink}></a>
                18. Contact
            </h2>
            <p>
                For questions about these Terms, contact <a
                    href="mailto:customer-support@netmind.ai"
                    >customer-support@netmind.ai</a
                >.
            </p>
        </div>
    </article>
</BaseLayout>
